+ * already reads, so that its idle exit can dispatch host descriptor events
+ * for a CPU0 that is late (see darwin_irq_dispatch()).  No vector is raised
+ * and no signal is sent, so a CPU running guest code is never interrupted.
+ * Only the IRQ notification thread calls it.  Returns 1 if a CPU was woken, 0
+ * if none is idle, and -1 if there is no secondary CPU.
